    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-054 — transform: rotate().** One commit. **Docs follow after merge.**\n\nFirst cycle shipped under the new **\"synthetic-fixture verified\"** category: rotate is not used in production Wikipedia (the only transform reaching cascade is `translateY(-50%)` on the magnifier, deferred on `parent_content_height`), but the primitive is architecturally useful and verified via a permanent fixture.\n\n## What shipped\n\nFour layers, each confirmed absent by measurement:\n\n| Layer | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `parse_angle()` | Not present — `parse_length` is pixels only | New function: deg/rad/turn/grad/unitless → degrees |\n| `transform` in whitelist | Not present — parser drops it | Whitelisted |\n| `LayoutBox::transform_rotate_deg` | Not present | `float = 0.0f`, set by `layout_element` |\n| `paint_box` rotate | Zero `cairo_rotate` calls | `cairo_save/translate(cx,cy)/rotate/translate(-cx,-cy)/restore` wrapping the whole body |\n\n**Design decisions:**\n\n- **Wrap the ENTIRE `paint_box` body** (bg, border, shadow, mask, content, children) — CSS transform affects rendered pixels, not just children\n- **Extract first `rotate()` only** — `translateY(-50%)` → field=0 → zero paint delta → zero Wikipedia regression\n- **`transform-origin` always 50% 50%** (box center) — custom origins deferred\n\n## The fixture (permanent reproducibility asset)\n\n`docs/adr054-rotate-test.html` — three stacked boxes:\n\n```\nControl: upright orange square\nrotate(45deg): orange diamond\nrotate(30deg) rectangle: tilted blue rectangle\n```\n\nVerified visually — all three render correctly. The diamond corners are exactly at the rotated positions; the tilted rectangle shows a non-45° angle.\n\n**Note on the fixture**: uses `background-color:` / `border-width:` / `border-style:` / `border-color:` longhand. The shorthand forms (`background: #d35400`, `border: 2px solid #333`) **don't parse yet** in HoneyBee — that's a separate pre-existing parser gap, not ADR-054. Documented in the fixture itself so future contributors using shorthand know to expect it.\n\n## Verified delta\n\n**Synthetic fixture: 3 boxes render with correct rotation.** Screenshot at 2026-11-01 confirmed:\n- Upright control square\n- Orange diamond (rotate 45deg)\n- Tilted blue rectangle (rotate 30deg)\n\n**Zero production PNG delta.** Wikipedia's `translateY(-50%)` on the magnifier is parsed but not rotated (rotate parser skips it). Before/after screenshots on the HTML article: identical.\n\n## Test count\n\n- 647 → 651 cases (+4 new)\n- 2471 → 2490 assertions (+19)\n- 4 new tests:\n  - `parse_angle` unit (deg/rad/turn/grad/unitless)\n  - `layout: rotate(45deg)` → field 45\n  - `layout: no transform` → field 0\n  - `layout: translateY(-50%)` → field 0 (regression safety)\n\n## What this delivers\n\n- **First cycle with a visible synthetic-fixture delta** — the new verification category has its proof\n- **New verification category established**: \"synthetic-fixture verified\" — structurally same rigor as \"scroll-PNG verified\" but uses `file://` + local `http.server` fixture instead of a scroll position\n- **Future translate() ADR is now trivial** — the paint wrapper is in place; translate just adds another Cairo operation in the same wrapper\n\n## Out of scope (future ADRs)\n\n- `translate()` / `translateX()` / `translateY()` — blocked on `parent_content_height` (magnifier would land at y=-3 without `top: 50%`)\n- `scale()` / `matrix()` — different paint operations\n- `transform-origin` custom values\n- `transform` on `<img>` (early-return path limitation)\n- **Background/border shorthand parsing** — the fixture bypass revealed this gap; separate ADR needed\n\nRefs #243\n",
